/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_118.md:69:**This finding is DEFERRED until F1 is resolved.** The "lambda general form" assertion (item 3 below) depends on the sign chosen in F1. Codex should **not** apply F2 until the orchestrator confirms F1's resolution. If the user picks F1 direction (a), apply F2 below as written. If the user picks (b) or (c), the F2 instructions are updated accordingly in a follow-up directive.
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_118.md:71:**Required change (assuming F1 direction (a) — minus sign):**
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_118.md:91:3. **lambda general-form assertion** (sign per F1 direction (a)). After SymPy line 101 (after the existing `lam_uniform - …` assertion, which under F1(a) will have been flipped to `lam_uniform + …`):
