/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_123.md:34:  > `\Xi_v^{F1} = -\frac{3\sqrt{30}\,\pi^{3/2}}{228}\,\mathfrak r_{F1} \approx -1.01675633282526.`
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_123.md:44:The notes' boxed symbolic constant is `228` but the same notes' boxed numeric `Xi_v^{F1} ≈ -1.01675633282526` is only consistent with denominator `160`. The script's independent re-derivation from `Ks`, `Kq`, `lam` yields `160` and the numeric `-1.01675633282526...` to 20 digits. Which is correct?
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_123.md:46:- Manual check: with `r_{F1} = sqrt(12*(37/20)^2/pi^2 - 1) ≈ 1.7779`,
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_123.md:47:  - `-3*sqrt(30)*pi^(3/2)*r_{F1}/160 ≈ -1.0168` (matches the boxed numeric)
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_123.md:48:  - `-3*sqrt(30)*pi^(3/2)*r_{F1}/228 ≈ -0.713`  (does NOT match the boxed numeric)
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_123.md:54:- (b) `228` is correct. Then BOTH the script (line 46) AND the notes' numerical box `-1.01675633282526` are wrong; the upstream `lam` definition or one of `Ks`, `Kq` would need to be re-derived from stages 220-221 to produce `228`. This would also cascade into the numeric Xi_v^F1 quoted by the notes and likely into downstream stages 125-139.
