/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/stage_006_delta_iter3.md:12:Iteration 2 blocked because F2(c) as originally written was mathematically wrong: setting `Z=1` does NOT kill the projected leak in this script. Reason: `Wgp = sp.diff(Wg, w)` is odd in `w`, `Fw1 = w` is odd, so `Wgp · 1 · Fw1` is even and integrates to a nonzero value. The auditor's "trivial mediator kills the leak" claim was incorrect.
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/stage_006_delta_iter3.md:16:This delta re-applies F2(a) and F2(b) from iter 2, plus the corrected F2(c).
/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/stage_006_delta_iter3.md:20:After editing, RUN `python3 <path>` and confirm exit 0 with all assertions passing. Iterate edit → run → diagnose until clean. If the script still won't run cleanly after ~5 attempts, append `## Blocked: F2-iter3` with a specific question instead of thrashing. The verifier reviews substance afterward, not whether the script runs.
