    18	### F3 — hardcoded_result (D/N eigenvalue derivation)
    19	**Classification:** resolved.
    20	SymPy lines 24-47 introduce `q(x)=sin(k x)`, verify `q''+k²q=0`, `q(0)=0`, `q'(L_W)=0` at `k_W=π/(2 L_W)`, then build `Omega_W=k_W c_s` and assert `kappa0_derived - 4 L_W²/(π² a²) = 0`. `kappa0_from_tube` is reassigned to `kappa0_derived` at line 51. Mathematica `.wl` lines 34-55 mirror this. Outputs show the four new PASS lines in both engines.
    21	
    22	### F1 — tautological_check (kappa0_bare round-trip)
    23	**Classification:** resolved.
    24	SymPy lines 64-69 compute `kappa0_bare_geom = 4 L_W_required²/(π² a²)` and assert it equals `(1+r_c)/3`; `kappa_c` is now derived from this round-trip (line 71). Mathematica lines 62-66 mirror this. New non-tautological assertions appear in both transcripts.
    25	
    26	### F2 — tautological_check (gamma0 extraction)
    27	**Classification:** resolved.
    28	SymPy line 79 uses `gamma0_from_D = sp.I * D_bare.coeff(z, 5)` (orchestrator-corrected +I sign) and asserts equality with `(1+r_c)/9`; also adds `kappa0_from_D` extraction (line 89). Mathematica lines 73 and 78 mirror with `+I`. Sign analysis: `D_bare.coeff(z,5) = -i(1+r_c)/9`, so `+i · (-i(1+r_c)/9) = (1+r_c)/9` — correct. Outputs confirm both engines pass these new substantive coefficient-extraction checks.
    29	
    30	### F4 — insufficient_verification (SymPy tube-length assert)
    31	**Classification:** resolved.
    32	SymPy lines 59-62 add the missing `expect_zero("tube-length law: L_W = pi a sqrt((1+r_c)/3) / 2", ...)`. Mathematica retains its pre-existing line 60 assertion. Transcript shows `tube-length law: ... = 0`.
